  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 126 PM CDT Sat Aug 15 2026\n\nThe mid-level ridge over SE CONUS will move westward tomorrow \n(Sunday) and center over Texas, leading to increased subsidence, \nhot, and generally rain-free conditions through next work week. We \ncan't completely take out the chance for a couple showers or storms \ndeveloping along the afternoon seabreeze. Highs will continue to \nrange from 90 along the coast to 105 over the Brush Country, with \nheat indices peaking around 110 each afternoon over the Coastal \nPlains. Therefore a moderate to major risk of heat-related impacts \nwill continue over South Texas for the foreseeable future with UiL \nWBGT risks mainly moderate to occasionally high. In addition to heat \nconcerns, we'll be monitoring the potential for elevated fire \nweather conditions daily over the Brush Country where winds over 20 \nmph may coincide with relative humidity less than 30% in the \nafternoon to early evening hours.\n\nA mid to upper level trough over the Great Lakes region late next \nweek tries to extend south into Texas, but no direct influences are \nexpected over South Texas next weekend at this time. In fact, \nanother strong mid-level ridge may quickly replace and center over \nthe southern CONUS.",
